    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0458" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.04418/91a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Office of Arms and Munitions
                        Control</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Green</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of the
                        Special Committee of the Senate Investigating the Munitions Industry</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Rausenbush</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-04">December 4,
                        1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Raushenbush</hi>: In compliance with your
                    suggestion I enclose a text of a suggested amendment to Section 2 of the
                    Neutrality Act.</p>
                <p>If, instead of amending the Neutrality Act, it is desired to rewrite it entirely
                    as a new Act, the only changes necessary in the enclosed text would be the
                    following: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Omit: “That Section 2 of the Joint Resolution of Congress (S. J. Res.
                            173) approved August 31, 1935, be and the same is hereby amended to read
                            as follows:”</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Change the first sentence of paragraph (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >a</hi>) to read: “The term ‘Board’ means the National Munitions Control
                            Board which was established pursuant to Section 2 of the Joint
                            Resolution approved August 31, 1935 (Pub. Res.—No. 67—74th
                            Congress.)”</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Add to paragraph (<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>): <hi
                                rendition="#italic">“Provided, however</hi>, that persons who have
                            registered pursuant to Section 2 of the Joint Resolution of Congress
                            approved August 31, 1935 (Pub. Res.—No. 67—74th Congress), shall not be
                            required, during the period that such registration remains valid, to
                            register under this Act.”</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Green</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d246-a1.xml" xpointer="d246-a1"/>
